{{also|téléportation}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined by [[w:Charles Fort|Charles Fort]] in his 1931 book ''[[w:Lo!|Lo!]]'' from {{prefix|en|tele|transportation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-teleporation.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many (mostly [[hypothetical]] or [[fictional]]) processes of [[move|moving]] matter from one [[spatial]] point to another without physically [[cross]]ing the space [[in between]] and which are often [[depict]]ed or [[describe]]d as happening [[instantaneously]], and through [[dematerialization]] or [[gateway]]s.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|teleport}}
* {{l|en|teletransportation}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|teleport}}
* {{l|en|quantum teleportation}}

